+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+A task can only be referred to by its title, and a title changes when the task is renamed. The app needs a stable reference that survives a rename.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets an `id`: a string no other task of the list has. It never changes (rename, tag, complete, reopen keep it).
+- `add` returns the task with its `id`.
+- The list gets `get(id)`, returning `Result<Task>` (`not-found` for an unknown id).
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept a task's id as well as its title.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-identity`: unique, stable task ids, lookup by id, and id accepted wherever a title identifies a task.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- Rules touched: "No wall clock or randomness in the domain" (ids are generated from a per-list counter, not from the clock or random values); "Errors are returned as a Result" (`get` and id lookups return `not-found`, nothing throws); TSDoc on exported functions; no new runtime dependency.
+- Public API in `src/index.ts`: the exported `Task` type gains `id` and `TaskList` gains `get`. No new export is needed.
+- Code: `src/domain/task.ts`, `src/domain/list.ts`, `test/list.test.ts`.
